    Ministry of Economy: accountable for every scarce resource, not only model funding
    
    Founder directive: the Ministry's mandate is broadened to ensure the availability
    of other resources such as disk space, and to take action.
    
    - Act 29 section 6 "Resource availability": the Ministry is the accountable
      Executive owner of disk, inodes, memory headroom, load and Town state growth.
      It forecasts time to exhaustion, acts before shortage at thresholds earlier than
      the Janitor's, directs the Janitor (Act 12) and Resource Safety guard (Act 13) as
      its instruments, and escalates what it cannot fix as NEEDS-FOUNDER. The safety
      rules of Acts 12 and 13 are unchanged and bind the Ministry.
    - economy-resources.py (no model call): measures filesystems, inodes, cgroup
      memory headroom and load, keeps a 14-day history, forecasts hours to full, and at
      watch/short/critical runs the Janitor pipeline (inventory, classify,
      scratch-quarantine, quarantine, reclaim-idle-caches, reclaim, reclaim-quarantined)
      with logging. It never deletes anything itself.
    - executive-economy-cycle.sh refreshes resources every 30 minutes (10 while short),
      dispatches the Ministry's agent every 2 hours instead of 12 while short, and
      wakes it only on a change of status, not on a percentage drifting.
    - Mandate, BRANCHES.md and the daily digest line (resources, NEEDS-FOUNDER) updated.
    - boot-smoke expects the Ministry's dispatch now that Act 29 is committed.
    - New smoke test economy-resources-smoke.sh and cycle assertions.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
